DTEND:20270122T180000Z
SUMMARY:Olio Family Vacay Guatemala: From Antigua to Lake Atitlán
DESCRIPTION:OlioTrips are open to everyone and we foster the spirit of mean
 ingful connections\, new experiences and a space where you can be at ease.
  Think family vacation but with a chosen family (and without the bickering
  😂). In 2024\, Antigua became an extension of the Olio ecosystem.That y
 ear we spent a month in Guatemala running two OlioTrips\, and our favorite
  part (besides swimming in Lake Atitlán) was how our group got the chance
  to connect and bond with locals: the artists\, musicians\, business owner
 s\, and teachers we met along the way\, the house parties and homestyle di
 nners we were welcomed into.We're tied in with friends who run venues and 
 community projects similar to Olio\, and we've stayed in touch since the l
 ast trip. Those friends are onto all kinds of new projects\, and they've t
 old us that when we come back\, this trip will be even better than the las
 t.Nothing leaves us more recharged and inspired than time in Antigua\, fol
 lowed by the quiet integration that Lake Atitlán offers. Our last trip th
 ere is what inspired us to open our own venue\, and we think it's time tha
 t Olio goes back to Guatemala.Our dear friend\, Mayte Oliva\, cultural pro
 ducer\, photographer\, designer\, and all-around lovely human being\, will
  be with us for the entirety of the trip. She'll welcome and guide us thro
 ugh experiences that we would never see on our own\, and have us belly lau
 ghing throughout.Flow of the trip: Antigua - Jan 15 - 19thThis time\, we'r
 e settling into a gorgeous home in Antigua for the first half of the trip.
  Days are for workshops at our friend’s artist residency\, chef-prepared
  meals in a local architect’s orchid garden\, or wandering the dreamy st
 reets of this UNESCO-listed town\; nights are for inviting artists and loc
 als over for dinners\, dancing\, renting out the local movie theater\, sal
 ons\, and intimate house concerts.Lake Atitlan - Jan 19th - 22ndThen we mo
 ve to the lake\, where the pace slows even further. Some of us will relax 
 and take it all in\; others will join a sunrise hike or a cooking workshop
 . Either way\, we'll share meals\, play games\, and make a new group of be
 st friends before heading home restored.Selfishly\, we can't wait to go ba
 ck and we can't wait to share this world with you: swimming through the he
 at of the day\, visiting our friends' studios and restaurants\, and baskin
 g in new friendships as artists and teachers we love come to us for house 
 concerts and shared meals.We've built this trip to move slowly so that we 
 come home recharged and inspired. Welcome to Guatemala!&nbsp\;Some highlig
 hts to expect:Ridiculously good coffee&nbsp\;Courtyard breakfasts in Antig
 uaPlenty of free time to wander the shops\, cafes and restaurantsPottery a
 nd weaving workshop at Red MateriaGuided conversations that help us contex
 tualize and process our new learningsLakefront accommodations in AtitlanVo
 lcano views and optional volcano hikeOptional sunrise hikeLake kayaking&nb
 sp\;--Full price for the 8 day trip: Shared room $2750. Private Room $3350
 . Duo $5\,300 for two\, or ($2\,650/person)$500 deposit to reserve your sp
 ot!Balance to be paid in full by Dec 1.Reach out for payment plan options.
  Included:Accommodations (7 nights)All breakfasts + 5 additional mealsMajo
 rity of workshops\, tours\, and activitiesTransportation to/from activitie
 sTips for drivers &amp\; guides Not Included:Flights to/from GuatemalaMeal
 s not listedTravel insurancePersonal expenses---What kind of traveler is t
 his trip for?This trip is for people who want to experience Guatemala as i
 f they were visiting a local friend. You want to see places and meet peopl
 e that would probably never happen were you to go on your own. All of our 
 guides and friends in Antigua speak English\, so language wont be a barrie
 r - but if you do speak Spanish all the better!This is the right trip if y
 ou:Enjoy the blend of curiosity and social life that defines an Olio. Work
 shops and wandering by day\, dinners\, salons and house concerts by night.
 Are drawn to Antigua's mix of colonial streets\, artist studios\, and crea
 tive community.Want a good amount of unstructured time built in and not ju
 st a packed itinerary. Space to wander\, rest by the lake\, linger at a lo
 ng lunch or follow a conversation wherever it goes.Enjoy small groups wher
 e you'll actually get to know everyone by the end. That’s why we call it
  a family vacay!This trip works well whether you're coming solo or with a 
 friend. Most Olio travelers come alone\, and the group itself becomes the 
 reason you’ll want to come on the next trip!In their own words\, travele
 rs from our last Guatemala trip:"Amigos\, before I get back into my New Yo
 rk flow: Thank you so much for such a beautiful trip. It fulfilled so much
  of what I want all the time but especially what I need right now—time o
 utside (and in the water\, swoon)\; with people who are lovely and interes
 ting who can take me out of my world\; and getting out of my head and into
  joy\, sun\, and community."- Pilar"Thanks to the Olio team for organizing
 \, guiding\, and supporting us during the trip! Thanks to everyone for the
  meaningful and fun conversations as well. This trip surpassed every expec
 tation I had\, allowed me to fully pause my work life\, validate things I'
 ve been thinking about\, generate new work and non-work ideas\, and enjoy 
 and learn about everything we did."- Ritesh"Shoutout to @think.olio and a 
 very special group of people who provided me the space to experience and b
 e witness to love\, care\, connection\, joy\, vulnerability\, humility\, h
 ealing\, wonder\, and so much goddamn fun. I was inspired by the resistanc
 e\, resiliency and ancestral veneration as a daily practice. This trip was
  a beautiful life lesson in showing up\, and letting life surprise you."- 
 NicoleAccommodations(Think boutique accommodations - not luxury but defini
 tely grown up and very comfortable)Antigua: We'll be based at two gorgeous
  properties that are an attraction in themselves and also an easy walk int
 o Antigua's UNESCO-listed streets.Lake Atitlán: We move to our accommodat
 ions right on the lake with gardens\, hammocks\, a pool\, kayaks\, and a p
 rivate organic garden and meals.How rooming works:Shared Room ($2\,750) 
 — You'll room with another Olio traveler. If you're coming solo\, we'll 
 match you thoughtfully (most of our travelers come this way).Private Room 
 ($3\,350) — Your own room for the whole trip\, subject to availability.D
 uo ($5\,300 for two\, or $2\,650/person) — Coming with a friend or partn
 er? Book together and each save $100 off the shared rate. We’ll have opt
 ions to share a bed or to have separate beds in a shared room.Room availab
 ility at both properties is limited\, so we recommend booking early\, espe
 cially if you're set on a private room.\n\nTickets & info: https://www.vie
 wcy.com/event/oliotrip_guatemala_o
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/oliotrip_guatemala_o
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
